WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.130
On I go, searching for...

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.330
The past that was stolen from me

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.420
Wandering on through...

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.130
This city, so strange to see

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.080
Choked by the scent of flames that seems to...

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.880
Cling to me

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.630
Didn't we both say our goodbyes...

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.540
And go our separate ways?

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.790
When you see the face of hell...

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.330
It will squeeze your heart dry

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.750
Fighting on seems so pointless now

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.540
If this must be my fate...

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.790
Then I'll make my mind up now

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.960
So, please, won't you just leave me be...

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.750
Another day

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.250
Oh, will tomorrow hold something new to see?

00:01:41.080 --> 00:01:44.040
You're going to ignore the Society's orders?!

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:47.130
We can't let Ypsilon fight him again!

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:52.130
Our orders to discover the extent of
his combat abilites come first.

00:01:52.130 --> 00:01:56.130
That's why we were sent here. Right, Arron?

00:01:56.750 --> 00:01:59.920
And you think you can still do it
now that he's recovered.

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:03.540
Circumstances have granted us
a grand opportunity.

00:02:03.540 --> 00:02:07.000
And as scientists, we can't let
this opportunity slip away.

00:02:07.250 --> 00:02:10.250
Proto One has already been
taken by the Balarant!

00:02:10.710 --> 00:02:14.750
If we lose Ypsilon as well,
the Society will never forgive us!

00:02:14.750 --> 00:02:17.540
You're only thinking in terms of
your responsibilities.

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:20.920
Of course! I'm the captain of the Teltain!

00:02:20.920 --> 00:02:24.960
And Ypsilon is our responsibility!

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:27.210
Your responsibilities do not override ours.

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:30.250
If we lose Ypsilon, it's all over!

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.880
Don't worry, sir.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:34.040
Ypsilon is perfect.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:35.790
Trust us.

00:02:35.790 --> 00:02:38.880
I don't underestimate Chirico.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:41.130
Their past engagements have taught me that!

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:43.080
Yes, Chirico is quite powerful.

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:47.750
But he isn't good enough to beat Ypsilon now.

00:02:47.750 --> 00:02:52.790
Even after I've told you that he has
a Balarant battle group backing him?!

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:54.670
Ypsilon is perfect.

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:57.580
Their numbers do not matter.

00:02:57.830 --> 00:03:01.420
It's my responsibility to stop him
from returning to battle!

00:03:01.420 --> 00:03:03.000
Impossible, sir.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.830
We may never get another battle
between them again.

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:08.710
Yes, the timing for this is excellent.

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:11.380
We mustn't shirk our responsibilities.

00:03:14.130 --> 00:03:19.130
Perfect Soldier

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:38.290
Where will the rematch be?

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:41.040
Why won't you tell me?

00:03:41.290 --> 00:03:42.880
I'll tell you when the time comes.

00:03:43.880 --> 00:03:46.790
Do you think I'll try to set you up?

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:53.420
No matter. I just don't want anything
to interfere with this.

00:03:54.290 --> 00:03:55.790
You fight as you see fit.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:03:59.420
The final battle...

00:03:59.420 --> 00:04:01.460
How I've waited for this.

00:04:03.420 --> 00:04:05.170
Does it amuse you so much?

00:04:06.210 --> 00:04:08.500
Seeing me and Ypsilon fight.

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:09.960
Amuse?

00:04:09.960 --> 00:04:12.040
I don't think that's quite the right word.

00:04:13.670 --> 00:04:17.290
I doubt you want us to fight
just for your pleasure.

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:22.540
You're saying I have some other motive?

00:04:23.920 --> 00:04:25.290
You're saying you don't?

00:04:45.170 --> 00:04:47.170
He seems unusually calm.

00:04:47.170 --> 00:04:49.540
Before a big battle.

00:04:49.540 --> 00:04:51.330
That's very encouraging.

00:04:56.460 --> 00:04:58.540
I know you can do this!

00:04:59.080 --> 00:05:02.920
Please, don't let them fight each other!

00:05:02.920 --> 00:05:04.210
Impossible.

00:05:05.500 --> 00:05:09.130
He fought Ypsilon already
because he promised you!

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:11.130
This could end up with Chirico getting killed!

00:05:11.130 --> 00:05:12.960
Save your breath.

00:05:13.670 --> 00:05:14.960
Do you understand?

00:05:15.420 --> 00:05:18.920
Chirico and Ypsilon swore to have a rematch.

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:22.710
They're enemies who have to settle this.

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:26.250
The question is whether I should
interfere a second time.

00:05:26.250 --> 00:05:28.210
You're the cause of all this!

00:05:29.040 --> 00:05:29.920
You're wrong!

00:05:30.670 --> 00:05:34.920
You just want to be sure about Chirico, and so...

00:05:35.580 --> 00:05:38.830
And you don't want to know for sure?

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:42.630
No...

00:05:43.750 --> 00:05:45.040
I...

00:05:45.040 --> 00:05:46.790
You love him?

00:05:48.290 --> 00:05:51.460
I couldn't care less about your feelings in this.

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:55.580
As you say, I have an extreme interest in Chirico.

00:05:55.580 --> 00:05:58.380
His winning or losing will decide everything.

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:01.750
You don't know anything about Chirico.

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:04.000
How this is tearing him apart.

00:06:05.250 --> 00:06:08.670
Chirico will realize his destiny.

00:06:31.500 --> 00:06:33.830
I'm scared.

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:37.130
Why do you both have to...?

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:40.170
You don't have to worry.

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:41.960
Rochina will protect you.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:44.790
No! That's not what I mean!

00:06:45.290 --> 00:06:47.420
Ypsilon said it himself.

00:06:48.130 --> 00:06:50.710
You're the only other one like him.

00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:54.710
I think he's lonely.

00:06:55.040 --> 00:06:57.670
Chirico, please... Don't go.

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:05.040
I don't know why, but I have to.

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:29.170
You're disobeying orders! Ypsilon, come back!

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:30.790
Ypsilon, do you read me?!

00:07:33.170 --> 00:07:34.880
I don't believe this!

00:07:34.880 --> 00:07:36.210
Why didn't you stop him?!

00:07:36.210 --> 00:07:38.380
Quite impossible, sir.

00:07:38.380 --> 00:07:39.880
The arrow has sprung from its bow.

00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:42.750
I can't allow this! Recall him at once!

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:44.710
Let's go, Gurran.

00:07:44.710 --> 00:07:48.920
Yes, brother. Scientists must verify
their experimental data.

00:07:48.920 --> 00:07:50.130
With their own eyes.

00:07:50.130 --> 00:07:51.420
To the battle.

00:08:14.380 --> 00:08:19.750
Whatever the reason, we can't allow these battles
to continue in the Nonaggression Zone!

00:08:19.750 --> 00:08:24.040
They may have disguised their ships,
but the Balarant are definitely behind this!

00:08:24.460 --> 00:08:29.080
Do you remember those informal inquiries
about that mystery ship?

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:34.000
Yes. We told them it wasn't a Gilgamesh ship.

00:08:34.000 --> 00:08:35.080
What about it?

00:08:35.420 --> 00:08:38.170
Chirico and the Prototype were on that ship!

00:08:38.170 --> 00:08:39.000
What?!

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:40.380
That's not all.

00:08:40.380 --> 00:08:42.710
Since we had our doubts about the inquiries,

00:08:42.710 --> 00:08:45.880
we've monitored the radio transmissions
from planet Sunsa.

00:08:46.750 --> 00:08:49.790
Who do you think the
Balarant commander there is?

00:08:49.790 --> 00:08:52.460
Well, if they know about the Protoype...

00:08:52.460 --> 00:08:53.630
Someone big?

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:56.420
Major General Glass?
Lieutenant Colonel Gordon?

00:08:56.710 --> 00:08:58.210
Captain Rochina!

00:08:58.210 --> 00:08:59.460
Rochina?!

00:08:59.460 --> 00:09:02.170
As in OUR Captain Rochina?!

00:09:05.130 --> 00:09:08.710
A Gilgamesh officer becoming
a Balarant commander...

00:09:08.710 --> 00:09:10.290
I don't believe it!

00:09:10.290 --> 00:09:13.830
It's the truth! And it's your responsibility!

00:09:13.830 --> 00:09:16.830
He was assigned directly under you, wasn't he?

00:09:17.830 --> 00:09:21.540
I never could tell what he was really thinking.

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:26.750
Puts your political position at risk, eh, Battentain?

00:09:27.420 --> 00:09:29.000
Is that a threat?

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:31.670
Another surprising thing.

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:34.830
That decommissioned ship
that was stolen, the Teltain,

00:09:34.830 --> 00:09:37.710
is in the area around planet Sunsa!

00:09:38.790 --> 00:09:43.830
You're saying the Balarant have Chirico and
the Prototype and the Teltain is after them?

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:45.830
I can't think of any other explanation.

00:09:47.460 --> 00:09:50.580
Gilgamesh can't overlook what's happening!

00:09:51.830 --> 00:09:53.750
I'm glad you understand.

00:09:53.750 --> 00:09:56.710
I want this passed along to the
highest levels of your government.

00:09:56.710 --> 00:09:59.880
Scramble the 7th Mobile Space Fleet to Sunsa!

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:02.920
That could restart the Hundred Years War.

00:10:03.170 --> 00:10:05.290
That will depend on our opponents' reaction.

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:10.130
The plan is to confront the Balarant ships
and capture Rochina!

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:11.790
Understood. I'll pass it along.

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:15.500
This is Gilgamesh 7th Mobile Space Fleet.

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:17.500
We are en route to the
Nonaggression Zone at full speed.

00:10:17.500 --> 00:10:19.170
Please advise as to remainder of orders.

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:22.040
This is Gilgamesh 7th Mobile Space Fleet.

00:10:22.040 --> 00:10:24.420
HQ to 7th Mobile Space Fleet.

00:10:24.420 --> 00:10:27.540
Continue on course and go to DEFCON 3!

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:30.500
Mission details to follow. That is all!

00:10:30.500 --> 00:10:31.500
Roger!

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:00.420
We're leaving.

00:11:01.540 --> 00:11:02.540
Yes, sir.

00:11:02.920 --> 00:11:04.420
Don't you want to come?

00:11:06.250 --> 00:11:07.580
I will.

00:11:08.420 --> 00:11:12.290
Now, you will see the true face of Chirico Cuvie.

00:11:18.960 --> 00:11:21.580
Prepare forces for launch, but stand by.

00:11:21.830 --> 00:11:22.830
Sir?

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:26.130
The Teltain will probably come after Ypsilon.

00:11:26.130 --> 00:11:27.960
When it shows, launch!

00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:28.880
Aye, sir!

00:11:29.540 --> 00:11:31.040
They'll come, all right...

00:12:45.040 --> 00:12:46.330
Chirico!

00:12:46.630 --> 00:12:48.960
You can fight any way you want to.

00:12:48.960 --> 00:12:50.920
Anything you want to say?

00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:54.580
Yeah. I want your ATs to back off
while we're fighting.

00:12:54.580 --> 00:12:57.170
Understood. We won't interfere.

00:12:57.170 --> 00:12:58.540
That's all!

00:12:58.540 --> 00:12:59.710
Chirico...

00:14:10.880 --> 00:14:12.250
There's Chirico.

00:14:12.630 --> 00:14:15.000
But where's Ypsilon?

00:14:15.000 --> 00:14:16.710
He has a plan.

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:19.330
I can hardly wait.

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:20.920
I wish he'd come out!

00:15:12.290 --> 00:15:13.380
Chirico!

00:15:20.960 --> 00:15:21.880
He's here!

00:15:34.170 --> 00:15:36.040
Well played, Chirico!

00:15:36.040 --> 00:15:37.960
I thought I could kill you right off!

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:42.330
I hate you.

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:46.880
But it seems a shame for me, a PS,
to kill so skilled a soldier.

00:15:47.880 --> 00:15:51.960
Haven't you figured out
what being a PS really means?

00:15:51.960 --> 00:15:53.500
I couldn't care less!

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:58.000
I live to fight, to win! That is all!

00:15:58.380 --> 00:15:59.290
Die!

00:16:17.580 --> 00:16:20.830
Got him! I can follow his movements perfectly!

00:16:29.420 --> 00:16:30.250
Impossible!

00:16:32.710 --> 00:16:33.540
Chirico!

00:16:34.960 --> 00:16:37.380
Ypsilon's doing quite well.

00:16:37.380 --> 00:16:39.250
At last, a true PS.

00:16:39.250 --> 00:16:40.790
Yes. He'll win.

00:16:44.880 --> 00:16:45.920
Did that do it?

00:17:35.750 --> 00:17:38.000
You see? Chirico is a PS!

00:17:38.000 --> 00:17:39.380
You're wrong!

00:17:39.670 --> 00:17:41.830
Ypsilon is a full PS!

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:45.170
Can any normal human
fight one on even terms?!

00:17:45.170 --> 00:17:47.500
But Chirico's a normal human!

00:17:47.500 --> 00:17:49.460
He doesn't need jijirium!

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:51.880
Being a PS isn't about needing jijirium!

00:17:52.630 --> 00:17:54.750
It's all a question of ability.

00:17:55.420 --> 00:17:57.920
He has the abilities of a true PS!

00:17:59.420 --> 00:18:03.080
And Chirico will soon prove it. By killing Ypsilon!

00:18:03.080 --> 00:18:04.170
No!

00:18:04.880 --> 00:18:07.080
Wait! What are you doing?!

00:18:44.040 --> 00:18:45.630
Stop it, both of you!

00:18:45.630 --> 00:18:47.540
Fyana, what are you doing?!

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:49.920
Ypsilon can't move.

00:18:50.330 --> 00:18:54.210
If you try to hurt him, then I'll...!

00:19:00.420 --> 00:19:02.960
Proto One... Why?

00:19:03.380 --> 00:19:04.710
Why did you stop him?

00:19:06.420 --> 00:19:09.880
You were almost free of me.

00:19:10.380 --> 00:19:12.210
Fyana, stay out of this.

00:19:12.210 --> 00:19:13.880
If I don't kill him now...

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:15.210
No!

00:19:15.710 --> 00:19:18.250
Chirico, you're a PS, too!

00:19:18.790 --> 00:19:19.710
What?!

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:22.750
She just had to interfere.

00:19:22.750 --> 00:19:25.460
She may be a PS, but she's still a woman.

00:19:26.380 --> 00:19:29.630
He'll never believe what she's saying. Not now.

00:19:30.080 --> 00:19:35.750
You think any normal human
could fight a PS like Ypsilon?!

00:19:36.080 --> 00:19:37.630
What are you saying?

00:19:37.630 --> 00:19:40.830
I'm able to fight him because of my mission disk.

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:42.630
No, you're wrong.

00:19:42.630 --> 00:19:49.210
Even using that disk, a human would never
have reflexes fast enough to react!

00:19:53.750 --> 00:19:57.540
The disk's burned out, but I...

00:19:58.750 --> 00:20:02.750
My body isn't enhanced! How can I be a PS?!

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:05.460
But you are a PS! You are...

00:20:19.790 --> 00:20:23.500
Chirico... I've lost.

00:20:25.790 --> 00:20:27.830
We really were the same, after all.

00:20:32.420 --> 00:20:35.420
You really are a PS.

00:20:35.790 --> 00:20:36.880
No!

00:20:37.710 --> 00:20:39.380
You are!

00:20:40.290 --> 00:20:44.130
Otherwise, my pride wouldn't let me die...

00:20:45.830 --> 00:20:52.630
...knowing I'd lost... to a normal... man.

00:21:04.170 --> 00:21:05.750
Ypsilon...

00:21:06.920 --> 00:21:08.920
Poor, poor Ypsilon.

00:21:10.170 --> 00:21:13.380
Maybe, in the end, it was I who killed you.

00:21:15.330 --> 00:21:17.630
And you, Chirico...

00:21:38.830 --> 00:21:42.250
Space launch standing by!
Commencing countdown!

00:21:42.830 --> 00:21:43.880
Ten!

00:21:43.880 --> 00:21:44.880
Nine!

00:21:44.880 --> 00:21:45.880
Eight!

00:21:45.880 --> 00:21:46.880
Chirico...
Seven!

00:21:46.880 --> 00:21:47.880
Six!

00:21:47.880 --> 00:21:48.880
Five!

00:21:48.880 --> 00:21:49.790
Four!

00:21:49.790 --> 00:21:50.880
Three!

00:21:50.880 --> 00:21:51.880
Two!

00:21:51.880 --> 00:21:52.830
One!

00:21:52.830 --> 00:21:53.830
Zero!

00:22:07.630 --> 00:22:09.750
You are a PS.

00:22:09.750 --> 00:22:14.460
You want proof? Then go to planet Quent.

00:22:14.460 --> 00:22:16.210
Quent?

00:22:16.210 --> 00:22:18.580
There you will learn everything.

00:22:18.920 --> 00:22:21.170
Go and investigate it yourself.

00:22:21.170 --> 00:22:23.460
I'll take care of the Prototype.

00:22:23.920 --> 00:22:26.830
Set course for Quent!

00:22:26.830 --> 00:22:28.500
Go, Chirico!

00:22:32.080 --> 00:22:35.040
What was it that lay hidden in my past?

00:22:35.920 --> 00:22:38.670
I'd fought Ypsilon and won.

00:22:39.540 --> 00:22:41.330
But I couldn't believe it.

00:22:41.880 --> 00:22:45.330
There was no way I could be a PS.

00:22:46.920 --> 00:22:48.580
The planet Quent...

00:22:49.130 --> 00:22:51.790
What awaited me there?

00:22:54.290 --> 00:22:55.750
Next Episode

00:22:56.630 --> 00:23:00.170
From the beginning, he felt it.
Somewhere in his heart.

00:23:00.170 --> 00:23:02.540
A thirst behind the rage.

00:23:02.540 --> 00:23:05.500
A loneliness in the depths of his desire for battle.

00:23:06.080 --> 00:23:07.880
For friends who are like him.

00:23:07.880 --> 00:23:12.130
For all the things he's given up to survive.

00:23:12.630 --> 00:23:14.960
To listen for voices which will never be.

00:23:15.960 --> 00:23:18.040
Next time, "Friends"

00:23:18.290 --> 00:23:21.290
The next step will be for friends
who were freed before him.

00:23:19.830 --> 00:23:24.290
Friends

00:23:19.830 --> 00:23:24.290
Next Time

00:23:42.540 --> 00:23:46.000
Whenever I'm feeling lonely

00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:49.540
Whenever I'm feeling sad

00:23:49.540 --> 00:23:55.920
I can always see you floating in my mind

00:23:56.420 --> 00:23:59.960
Whenever I'm alone

00:23:59.960 --> 00:24:03.380
Whenever I long for you

00:24:03.380 --> 00:24:09.630
I can always feel you inside my heart

00:24:09.630 --> 00:24:13.130
No matter how far apart we may go

00:24:13.130 --> 00:24:16.540
No matter if my path should part from yours

00:24:16.710 --> 00:24:23.040
The memories of you seem to shine inside my heart...

00:24:23.420 --> 00:24:29.380
Brighter than any other light...
